[Narrator]
You stir in bed restlessly. It's been what, ten, eleven hours now? 

You open your crust-laden eyes and are met with the pitch-blackness of your bedroom ceiling.

[Protagonist]
Mmmm...
Mmrgh.

[Narrator]
You are so, so tired of being tired all the time. You’re exhausted. Exhausted in a way that sleep cannot possibly hope to fix.

[Protagonist]
I should get out of the house.

[Narrator]
And do what exactly?

[Protagonist]
You're right, but I've gotta at least eat something?

[Narrator]
With what appetite?

[Protagonist]
Right again. A shower would be nice...

[Protagonist]
You bring your elbows back and your head forward and make to get up; however, something stops you. An invisible something. A heavy something pinning you down. Whatever it is, it's like it's sitting on your stomach with all its weight.